1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,020
In this tutorial you will turn a

2
00:00:03,020 --> 00:00:05,609
draft tenancy contract into accounting
entries.

3
00:00:05,609 --> 00:00:08,629
Open Leases and select the prepared draft.

4
00:00:08,629 --> 00:00:11,649
A contract in RentAxis has two grids.

5
00:00:11,649 --> 00:00:14,238
The first is its charge lines.

6
00:00:14,238 --> 00:00:19,415
Each line names what is being charged, the
account the income or

7
00:00:19,415 --> 00:00:24,592
liability is credited to, the gross
amount, any discount, and the net.

8
00:00:24,592 --> 00:00:29,769
Rent, security deposit and administration
fee are separate lines because they behave

9
00:00:29,769 --> 00:00:34,947
differently: rent is recognised across the
term, a deposit is a liability

10
00:00:34,947 --> 00:00:39,692
you hold, and a fee is income the day you
post.

11
00:00:39,692 --> 00:00:44,007
The second grid is the cheque register for
this contract.

12
00:00:44,007 --> 00:00:47,890
Every row carries a posting date, a cheque
number,

13
00:00:47,890 --> 00:00:51,341
a maturity date, the drawer's bank, the
amount

14
00:00:51,341 --> 00:00:54,793
and a narration such as Rent, first
installment.

15
00:00:54,793 --> 00:00:59,970
Notice that the cheque grid adds up to
exactly the contract value.

16
00:00:59,970 --> 00:01:03,853
If it does not, posting is refused,
because the

17
00:01:03,853 --> 00:01:07,305
register is how the money is tracked and

18
00:01:07,305 --> 00:01:10,756
it has to account for all of it.

19
00:01:10,756 --> 00:01:15,502
Nothing you have looked at so far has
touched the ledger.

20
00:01:15,502 --> 00:01:18,522
The contract is still a draft, and

21
00:01:18,522 --> 00:01:21,111
a draft can be edited freely.

22
00:01:21,111 --> 00:01:22,405
Now select Post.

23
00:01:22,405 --> 00:01:24,131
Confirm the contract date.

24
00:01:24,131 --> 00:01:28,014
RentAxis writes one tenancy contract
journal debiting rent receivable

25
00:01:28,014 --> 00:01:31,897
and crediting each line's own account, and
one post-dated

26
00:01:31,897 --> 00:01:35,780
cheque journal for every row of the grid,
moving

27
00:01:35,780 --> 00:01:39,663
the amount from rent receivable into
post-dated cheques receivable.

28
00:01:39,663 --> 00:01:42,683
Open the Journals tab and read them.

29
00:01:42,683 --> 00:01:45,271
The contract status is now Active.

30
00:01:45,271 --> 00:01:47,429
Open the Recognition schedule tab.

31
00:01:47,429 --> 00:01:52,606
RentAxis has already planned how the rent
will be earned, one row

32
00:01:52,606 --> 00:01:57,352
per calendar month, using the actual
number of days in each.

33
00:01:57,352 --> 00:01:59,509
Nothing there is posted yet.

34
00:01:59,509 --> 00:02:04,686
Posting is deliberate: after a contract is
posted it is never edited,

35
00:02:04,686 --> 00:02:09,432
only amended, which reverses the original
and writes a fresh one.
